at files it under transport error a great deal.\"},{\"text\":\"A 429 refusal at the edge costs the platform almost nothing.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"When that cap is spent the gateway answers 429 at the edge — without waking the service behind it — so the refusal costs the platform almost nothing and costs a caller that files it under transport error a great deal.\"},{\"text\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds, and never against a connection.\"},{\"text\":\"Requests are counted over a fixed window of 60 seconds.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds, and never against a connection.\"},{\"text\":\"Requests are never counted against a connection.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds, and never against a connection.\"},{\"text\":\"Opening a second socket buys a caller nothing in terms of rate limit.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"Opening a second socket therefore buys a caller nothing.\"},{\"text\":\"A client spread across eight worker processes is throttled at exactly the point one process would have been.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"A client spread across eight worker processes is throttled at exactly the point one process would have been — and pays for the extra file descriptors as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window, and a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 requests in the same window.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window, and a credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"A refusal is not an outage.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"A refusal is not an outage, whatever the error class in a client library happens to call it.\"},{\"text\":\"A refusal is the platform declining to spend capacity that has already been promised to somebody else.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"It is the platform declining to spend capacity that has already been promised to somebody else, and waiting is the only correct answer.\"},{\"text\":\"Callers that retry at once are the largest single reason the cap exists.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"Callers that retry at once are the largest single reason the cap is there at all.\"},{\"text\":\"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\"},{\"text\":\"The Retry-After header value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\"},{\"text\":\"Waiting longer than the Retry-After header asks earns a caller no credit.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in.\"},{\"text\":\"The refusal body names the window the gateway counted in.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in.\"},{\"text\":\"The refusal body names the cap.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"It names the cap and the tier as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The refusal body names the tier.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"It names the cap and the tier as well.\"},{\"text\":\"The refusal body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused — nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\"},{\"text\":\"Nothing in the refusal body is meant for the retry loop.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body is there so that a human reading a log afterwards can see why the request was refused — nothing in it is meant for the retry loop.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway computes the wait with information the caller does not have.\",\"line\":19,\"span\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway computes the wait on the 503 path as well.\",\"line\":19,\"span\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 500 may be retried once the stated wait has passed.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 503 is the overload path.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"A batch credential is measured over exactly the same window as the default.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued and cannot be asked for per call.\"},{\"text\":\"The 